  "description": "BONQUU crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P 21 21 21. Reported CIF formula moiety: C72 H108 Er5 N6 Ni6 O51 3+,3(Cl1 O4 1-),15(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 9 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 9 O neighbors; Er5 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni4 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni6 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni5 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 19 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.426-3.915 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.87-115.54°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Er5Ni6(S-HL)6(AcO)3(μ3-OH)9(H2O)6](ClO4)3·15H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 9 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
